abstract: >
  Version 2.0 retains the April 2026 computational theorem
  f(3) >= 3.0084928720 at Z11 (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19722202) and records two
  subsequent extensions of the same Wróblewski pairing of Behrend sphere
  blocks. An interval-certified adaptive chain Z14–Z23 yields
  f(3) >= 3.008500752707. Eight exact-rational even-p Jensen steps Z25–Z32
  then produce the 18-place downward truncation
  f(3) >= 3.008500858304852623, conditional on the Z24 outward-rounded
  moment-certificate integers. The v1 implementation uses a Python driver
  with an embedded C kernel compiled at runtime, using unsigned __int128
  arithmetic and strtod() to handle overflow hazards at Z12 and beyond, and
  includes a floating-point error certificate confirming the Z11 margin
  exceeds the total IEEE 754 error bound by a factor exceeding 10^15.
